Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-14-2001||11:08 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TwisT:<BR><B>Had a sudden urge this afternoon to ask the Forum... <P>Does anyone have pictures,  or any suggestions/ ideas/ experience,  with making a Ferrari-like Fiero without use of a kit?<P>Do you look at the Fiero and see "Ferrari" like I do???  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Ive seen some attempts......they were awful. your second quest.......yes see below sig.<BR>You should, they copied most of the measurements from a real 308 they took apart.<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||TwisT||08-15-2001||03:22 AM||||Roger,<P>Thanks for the response.<P>"Ferrari-like" is bright red paint...  it is lowered suspension... it is 18" diameter polished-lip/ silver wheels...  it is a Momo steering wheel... LOL...  stuff like that.  I see the Fiero as this;  pure sports car.  Lot's of Italian stuff.  <P>Not long ago I talked to a gentleman about this... he had the same idea I had.  Keep it a Fiero,  but "Ferrari-ize" it.<P>Here's what I'm talking about...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stage2side.JPG"> <P>Picture shown with Stage 2 side scoop and lower panel,  Kid Danger front air-dam,  and 18" Antera 183 rims.  Wing is late-model Saleen...  don't care for it tho.  Would rather use the factory wing that is raked back.<P>See what I mean???<P>Brett||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-15-2001||10:44 AM||||pic is a little decieving, it is Ferrari Rossa Corsa red, I like most of your ideas, but Ferrari isnt that big on rear wings,F40 and F50 being exceptions. You seldom see any chrome except a few tiny emblems-means the wheels have to be painted.||||reg||1
